{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791119010,"nonce":"aSELPPerdbh9WLwIBuh0qTdAa2s=","title":"Canvas: a first-party \u003ccanvas\u003e element and vector drawing system","message":"A built-in \u003ccanvas\u003e element (HTML's) with an immediate-mode 2D drawing context, rendered on the GPU through ashui's own pipeline. It is the foundation for charts, and for anything else that draws rather than lays out. The model is Blinc's canvas element plus blinc_canvas_kit's Painter2D and Sketch. It is built Haxe-first, with its shader in hxsl.\n\n- `\u003ccanvas draw={(ctx, size) -\u003e ...}\u003e`: `ctx` is a 2D context modelled on HTML's CanvasRenderingContext2D, which web and Haxe developers already know.\n  - Paths: beginPath, moveTo, lineTo, quadraticCurveTo, bezierCurveTo, arc, arcTo, ellipse, rect, roundRect, closePath.\n  - Painting: fill and stroke with the nonzero or evenodd rule; fillRect, strokeRect, clearRect.\n  - State: fillStyle and strokeStyle (colours and gradients); lineWidth, lineCap, lineJoin, miterLimit, setLineDash; globalAlpha.\n  - Transforms and clips: save, restore, translate, rotate, scale, transform, setTransform; clip.\n  - Text later.\n- Reactive in Solid style: `draw` runs inside a tracked computation and runs again only when a signal it read changes. Size changes also redraw it.\n- `Painter`: Processing-style wrappers over the context, after Painter2D (current fill and stroke, push and pop, rect, circle, line, path).\n- `Sketch`: `setup` and `draw(ctx, t, dt)` every frame, clocked by AnimationScheduler, so recordings and tests are deterministic. State lives in the sketch object.\n\nThe current pipeline has 112-float records drawn as SDF quads, no triangle pipeline, no MSAA and no stencil. The canvas route:\n1. blinc_abi emits one PRIM_CANVAS placeholder record over a canvas node's content box, as image_record does for SVGs, through a `blinc_tree_set_canvas(node, slot)` setter. The placeholder carries the node's transform, clips, fades, clip-path, opacity and layers.\n2. Haxe, at sync time as Images.resolve does, expands each placeholder into path records and triangle vertices:\n   - one record per fill or stroke call, with its paint (solid or gradient rows) and its vertex range;\n   - the records and vertices are appended to the records texture after the native rows, as clip-path polygon points are.\n3. A PathShader (hxsl, imports Sdf) fetches vertices by vertex index. It places them through the record's affine, and in the fragment applies the paint, the per-vertex fringe coverage and the clip products. Renderer draws each path record non-indexed: renderDrawRange(vertexCount, 1, 0, record).\n\n- Paths are flattened at a tolerance scaled by on-screen scale, so they stay crisp when zoomed.\n- Fills: a convex fast path as a fan, and ear clipping for simple concave polygons and their holes. Neither overlaps, so translucent fills do not double-blend.\n- Strokes are expanded to triangles, with miter, round and bevel joins and butt, round and square caps.\n- Antialiasing is a 1px feathered fringe with coverage per vertex, as NanoVG does, independent of MSAA.\n\n1. Vector core: path, flattening, fill and stroke tessellation, fringe. Unit tests.\n2. Render plumbing: PRIM_CANVAS, expansion, PathShader. Pixel tests.\n3. \u003ccanvas\u003e element and the 2D context, with reactive redraw. Painter and Sketch. Snapshot and motion scenes.\n4. Canvas text, through the glyph atlas.\n5. Charts on top (line, bar, area, pie), in ashui.components.","files":null}]}